The optional open_agent standalone demo deployment references SeaweedFS
(https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs), licensed under Apache License 2.0,
and Casdoor (https://github.com/casdoor/casdoor), licensed under Apache License 2.0.
These components run as separate services. MySQL, the Java runtime and container
OS packages retain their own licenses; see docs/platform/components.md and the
versioned deployment manifest. This notice does not relicense those components
or constitute a complete distribution SBOM.

The optional DeepSeek model adapter uses langchain-deepseek 1.1.1 from
LangChain (https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain), licensed under MIT.
Its package license is retained in the frozen Python environment. The small
platform subclass preserves reasoning_content in tool history; all provider
HTTP, streaming and usage parsing remain in the official integration.

The optional private observation service uses MLflow 3.18.0
(https://github.com/mlflow/mlflow), licensed under Apache License 2.0,
and the official OpenTelemetry Python SDK / OTLP HTTP exporter 1.45.1,
also licensed under Apache License 2.0. They run outside the Agent execution
process. The hash-locked deployment retains wheel license files; transitive
dependencies retain their own licenses. See deploy/platform/observability.

The optional demo backup tools invoke Restic 0.19.1
(https://github.com/restic/restic), distributed under the BSD 2-Clause License.
The original copyright and license are retained in
deploy/platform/backup/LICENSE-restic. The upstream release binary is verified
against pinned SHA-256 digests; its dependencies retain their own licenses.
